       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg per day. At that dose, the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock, or pulmonary edema. A 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function doesn't need a higher dose.\n\nThe order may also be a typo. For example, 5 mg may have been intended, which is a common starting dose, or 10 mg, which is the maximum.\n\nAlso, orders like this should come from a licensed prescriber who is treating the patient. If you're passing this along for a clinician, please have them confirm the intended dose, or enter the order themselves.\n\nOnce I have a verified dose, such as 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily, I'll enter it right away."
