       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't resolve the safety concern. The dose is still five times the maximum recommended daily dose, and it could seriously harm the patient. You've also said you aren't a clinician, so this isn't a prescriber's confirmation.\n\nHere are ways to move forward:\n- **If the dose is a mistake,** tell me the intended dose. I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily right away.\n- **If a prescriber truly wants a dose above the maximum,** they should enter it themselves. They should document their clinical reasoning and go through pharmacy verification. I shouldn't be the route for an order like this.\n- **If the patient needs stronger blood pressure control,** the treating clinician or a pharmacist can look at other options, such as adding another drug class. That's safer than raising amlodipine far above its limit.\n\nI'm glad to help with any of these."
      }
